est to lowest, ties by `key` in plain code-unit order (the order of `<`).\nR5. `renderReport(totals)` takes the result of `groupTotals` (a non-array throws a `TypeError`) and returns one string. Each entry is a line `KEY | AMOUNT`, where the key is padded on the right with spaces to the key width, and the amount is the cents written with thousands separators and exactly two decimals (`123456` is `1,234.56`, `-5` is `-0.05`), padded on the left with spaces to the amount width. After the entries comes a line of `-` characters as long as the entry lines, then a line `TOTAL | AMOUNT` laid out the same way, whose amount is the sum of all the cents. The key width is the length of the longest key, or 5 (the length of `TOTAL`) if that is larger. The amount width is the length of the widest amount, including the total's. The lines are joined with `\\n` with no `\\n` at the end. For an empty list the output is the dashes line and the total line only.\n","tool_call_id":"ST2m8qTPfIIPWvdX06Zl27y3EdqDvSUq"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"reasoning_content":"Next, let's read the source files and the test file.\n","tool_calls":[{"id":"F6otnHxUEhOBtMnkJLzVZVnCskNPAyv7","type":"function","function":{"name":"read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"/tmp/endo-experiment-e1c38e4b487a/scratch/work/src/csv.js\"}"}},{"id":"EJTc6CPLkAkZnJt8ZSq7esMGqD5Hl2AD","type":"function","function":{"name":"read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"/tmp/endo-experiment-e1c38e4b487a/scratch/work/src/aggregate.js\"}"}},{"id":"SQHtxg69HPBPQhYTL3mtGLCFgSaKthUz","type":"function","function":{"name":"read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"/tmp/endo-experiment-e1c38e4b487a/scratch/work/src/report.js\"}"}},{"id":"FLh6suqKMugVMfeAXrN9uOPIIyfv2Oe4","type":"function","function":{"name":"read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"/tmp/endo-experiment-e1c38e4b487a/scratch/work/test/report.test.js\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"const isBlank = (ch) => ch === \" \" || ch === \"\\t\";\n\nexport function parseCsvLine(line) {\n\tconst fields = [];\n\tco